  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong reference point for the core multimodal hypothesis. config_002 pairs the most expressive encoders in each modality (scgpt for RNA, ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L for images) with transformer-based aggregation (more expressive than avgpool for combining multiprofile outputs) and standard concat fusion. This tests whether the full multimodal pipeline with learned, non-linear components in both branches can achieve high validation accuracy. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components (encoder choice, aggregation, fusion) to identify what drives performance. If it underperforms, it signals that complexity in one or more components is the bottleneck, guiding targeted follow-ups. This is the highest-information single experiment under a 10-run budget because it simultaneously validates the multimodal architecture, the encoder choices, and the aggregation strategy."
}

